---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii4_132",
  "series": "Band II 4 (1701 - 1707)",
  "seq": 132,
  "text": "<p> [[436.9]] <b>132. BARTHÉLEMY DES BOSSES AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[436.10]] Hildesheim, 21. Mai 1706. [128.135.] </b></p>\n<p> [[437.3]] Illustrissime Domine </p>\n<p> [[437.4]] Remitto libros quos mihi nuper commodaras; pro quibus ingentes habeo gratias. Lator est\n[[437.5]] unus e nostris qui post transactum Hannoverae octiduum ad nos revertetur. Pervolvi eos magna\n[[437.6]] cum voluptate, illum maxime, qui tuas in Pelissonii librum notas ejusque responsa complectitur,\n[[437.7]] in quo si aliud nihil profectum est, luculentum certe controversiae moderate tractandae specimen\n[[437.8]] utriusque partis disputatoribus exhibuistis. Quanquam nec multum a nobis abesse mihi\n[[437.9]] visus es, nam difficultates si quae restant, admissa semel infallibilitate ecclesiae, <Fn><i>Zu</i> infallibilitate ecclesiae <i>bemerkt Leibniz</i>: hanc non admitto nisi in necessariis ad salutem, sed diutissime Concilia Oecumenica non habemus</Fn> ut plurimum\n[[437.10]] evanescunt. Si enim in philosophia uti me alias verissime monebas, salvis multis difficultatibus\n[[437.11]] systemata stare possunt, id ipsum in religione quae obscuritatem cum certitudine conjunctam\n[[437.12]] habet, multo magis valere debet. Quod etiam scutum prophanorum philosophorum telis, aliquoties\n[[437.13]] opponit Jaquelotius in hoc ipso, quem remitto, libro. Praeiverat illustris Huetius, amicus\n[[437.14]] tuus in <i>demonstratione evangelica</i>, cujus haec verba sunt propositione quarta initio capitis\n[[437.15]] decimi quarti: <i>ea est demonstrationum ratio, ut veritatis inquisitione ac inventione contentae\n[[437.16]] contrariis argumentis respondere negligant; idque merito quoniam simplex est ac unica veritas,\n[[437.17]] eaque reperta ac demonstrata, quaecumque opponantur falsa esse necesse est</i>. Sed stultus ego\n[[437.18]] qui talia coram te disseram. Orandus potius pater luminum, ut quod in te coepit, perficiat. Quod\n[[437.19]] ego, omnium, qui te colunt, postremus, facio sedulo nec porro facere desinam. </p>\n<p> [[437.20]] In tua ad Nizolii librum dissertatione praeliminari notisque sparsas hinc inde definitiones\n[[437.21]] reperi, quae mihi salivam moverunt, caeterasque quas a te confectas ajebas, videndi desiderium\n[[437.22]] excitarunt. Pace tua, Vir Illustrissime, parum abest quin irascar historiae isti tuae, quae profundioribus\n[[437.23]] scientiis ad quas illustrandas natus es, te subducit, magna cum jactura boni publici,\n[[437.24]] imo si ausim dicere, gloriae tuae. Nam si de gloria agitur, cedo mihi praestantissimum, quem\n[[438.1]] voles, hujus aevi historicum, cujus cum laude Cartesius philosophicam suam famam permutare\n[[438.2]] vellet si viveret? Scio alios aliter affectos esse, sed et scio plurimos sentire mecum. </p>\n<p> [[438.3]] A nupero colloquio nostro duae in mentem venere dubitationes quas hic subnecto, tuque\n[[438.4]] pro tua humanitate boni consules. </p>\n<p> [[438.5]] 1. Admissis diversae naturae entelechiis, quid opus est cognitione in brutis? An non\n[[438.6]] diversitas motuum, quam in illis cernimus, in diversas, sed perceptionis expertes entelechias\n[[438.7]] refundi poterit ad eum fere modum quo motus humani corporis negas pendere ab influxu\n[[438.8]] animae saltem ut perceptiva est? </p>\n<p> [[438.9]] 2. Cum caeteris paribus diversus corporis motus prodire non possit nisi a diversa entelechia,\n[[438.10]] sequi videtur, <b>legem</b> illam quam S. Paulus <b>videbat in membris suis, repugnantem\n[[438.11]] legi mentis suae, et captivantem se in lege peccati quae erat in membris\n[[438.12]] ejus,</b> hanc inquam legem, imo ipsum peccatum originale, quod vel haec ipsa lex est, uti a\n[[438.13]] multis protestantibus asseritur, vel hujus legis radix est, esse Entelechiam quandam, adeoque\n[[438.14]] substantiam vel substantialem uti Flaccius Illyricus asserebat. Sane motus illi concupiscentiae,\n[[438.15]] imo nec concupiscentia ipsa inordinata futura erat in natura integra. Quid quod, cum anima ita\n[[438.16]] corpori attemperata sit ut cuilibet motui corporis saltem a nobis perceptibili alius in anima\n[[438.17]] respondeat non liber, fiet ut animam hominis labe originali inquinandi et lege peccati quae est\n[[438.18]] in membris nostris captivandi, aliam omnino esse ab ea necesse sit quae in statu naturae\n[[438.19]] integrae creanda fuisset. Adeoque neminem omnium qui nunc creantur creandum fuisse, imo\n[[438.20]] nec creari potuisse si Adam non peccasset. Imo nec Adamum fortasse potuisse condi eundem si\n[[438.21]] peccaturus non fuerat. </p>\n<p> [[438.22]] Ptolomaeum tuum sacrorum rituum Consultorem a Pontifice creatum esse Roma nuper\n[[438.23]] accepimus. Erit forsitan hic ad altiora gradus. </p>\n<p> [[438.24]] Ecquando tandem litteras ad Papebrochium? Jam dudum expecto eas avide, ut hoc saltem\n[[438.25]] levi obsequio, quando aliter nequeo, benevolentiam honoremque immerenti exhibitos rependere\n[[438.26]] possim </p>\n<p> [[438.27]] Illustrissimae Dominationis tuae Humillimus et obedientissimus in Christo Servus </p>\n<p> [[438.28]] Bartholomaeus Des Bosses S J. </p>\n<p> [[438.29]] Hildesiae 21 Maji 1706. </p>\n",
  "number": "132.",
  "title": "BARTHÉLEMY DES BOSSES AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "Hildesheim, 21. Mai 1706. [128.135.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:132. BARTHÉLEMY DES BOSSES AN LEIBNIZ Hildesheim, 21. Mai 1706. [128.135.] Illustrissime Domine Remitto libros quos mihi nuper commodaras; pro quibus ingentes habeo gratias. Lator est unus e nostris qui post transactum Hannoverae octiduum ad nos revertetur. Pervolvi eos magna cum voluptate, illum ma...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>